          "identity_text": "Sapiens: A Brief History of Humankind (Hebrew: \u05e7\u05d9\u05e6\u05d5\u05e8 \u05ea\u05d5\u05dc\u05d3\u05d5\u05ea \u05d4\u05d0\u05e0\u05d5\u05e9\u05d5\u05ea, Qitzur Toldot ha-Enoshut) is a 2011 book by the Israeli military historian Yuval Noah Harari, based on a series of lectures he gave at the Hebrew University of Jerusalem. It was first published in Hebrew in Israel in 2011, and in English in 2014. The book surveys the history of humankind, beginning in the Stone Age and ending in the 21st century. The account relies on a fusion of the natural sciences with the social sciences.",
